Author: Aleš Matěj <amatej@redhat.com>
Date:   Wed Nov 11 12:31:04 2026 +0100

    Propagate rpm log messages not associated to callbacks when rpm ts fails
    
    Technically this can also show INFO and or DEBUG messages but when the
    transaction (or test transaction) fails in rpm I believe it is better to
    have as much information as possible.
    Otherwise the output says just `Transaction failed: Rpm transaction
    failed.` which is not helpful.
    
    For https://github.com/rpm-software-management/dnf5/issues/2028
    The failure due to missing `CAP_SYS_CHROOT` happens already in the test
    transaction but I think we should propagate the left over transaction
    logs also for the non-test transaction.
    
    Fix and enable test scenario for this behavior.

